---
import StaticSubmissionForm from "../components/StaticSubmissionForm.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Suggest church software"
  description="Suggest software for future independent research and provide official sources showing why it is relevant to churches in the UK."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Suggest software" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Future research</p>
      <h1>Suggest software</h1>
      <p class="measure">
        A suggestion is not a request for favourable coverage. Useful suggestions
        include an official website and evidence of relevance to UK churches.
      </p>
      <div class="prose measure">
        <h2>What to include</h2>
        <p>Give the product name, its official website and a brief explanation of the workflow it could support. If you know of current public documentation for pricing, Gift Aid, UK availability, data processing or exports, link to it rather than pasting supplier copy.</p>
        <h2>What happens next</h2>
        <p>Suggestions create a research lead, not a listing. The directory checks whether the product is relevant, whether its official site is active and whether the available evidence can support a useful, bounded profile. It may decide not to add a product or may retain open questions where evidence is incomplete.</p>
        <p>Use only public supplier information. Do not send church-member, pastoral, safeguarding, finance or other sensitive information.</p>
        <p>Before submitting, check whether the product already appears in the <a href="/software/">directory</a>. If it does, use the <a href="/supplier-update/">supplier update page</a> for a specific factual change instead of creating a duplicate research request.</p>
      </div>
      <StaticSubmissionForm kind="suggest" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
